From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: OddBlueDog <3959851+OddBlueDog@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 21:27:47 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: mt76: mt7915: serialize station statistics queries with
 resets

mt7915_sta_statistics() sends MCU queries that wait for a reply without
holding dev->mt76.mutex. During a full reset the firmware is reloaded
under that mutex after MT76_MCU_RESET has been cleared, so a station
dump at that moment queues a query in the middle of the firmware
download, times out, and makes the restart attempt fail and retry.

Take the mutex around the queries.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 mt7915/main.c | 7 +++++++
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+)

diff --git a/mt7915/main.c b/mt7915/main.c
index 8adbf480..43cdd3ad 100644
--- a/mt7915/main.c
+++ b/mt7915/main.c
@@ -1200,6 +1200,11 @@ static void mt7915_sta_statistics(struct ieee80211_hw *hw,
 	struct rate_info *txrate = &msta->wcid.rate;
 	struct rate_info rxrate = {};
 
+	/* serialize the MCU queries with mt7915_mac_full_reset(), which
+	 * reloads the firmware with this mutex held
+	 */
+	mutex_lock(&phy->dev->mt76.mutex);
+
 	if (!mt7915_mcu_get_rx_rate(phy, vif, sta, &rxrate)) {
 		sinfo->rxrate = rxrate;
 		sinfo->filled |= BIT_ULL(NL80211_STA_INFO_RX_BITRATE);
@@ -1241,6 +1246,8 @@ static void mt7915_sta_statistics(struct ieee80211_hw *hw,
 		}
 	}
 
+	mutex_unlock(&phy->dev->mt76.mutex);
+
 	sinfo->tx_failed = msta->wcid.stats.tx_failed;
 	sinfo->filled |= BIT_ULL(NL80211_STA_INFO_TX_FAILED);
 
